Patch X7 (rung 1b, gate G5): named harness steps in `cargo xtask ci --job test`.

The test job runs crash-json, version and live-input as steps of their
own, after known-answers and exit-codes, as amendments 14 to 17 of
docs/rungs/1b/PROGRESS.md give them (15 and 16 for `version`). A table,
`HARNESSES`, takes the place of the amendments' `tests(root, Some(..))`
calls. Each named step now writes its own log instead of overwriting the
workspace tests' one, and an xtask test checks that every step's test
file exists. X1 sets all four stamp variables, so amendment 16's extra
`version-set` build is left out. The session entry that added this file
says how it was tested.

Base: main at 106a8f0 with docs/rungs/1b/patches/x1-version-stamps.patch
applied. At the repo root, `git apply` X1 first and then this file; then
run `cargo xtask ci --job test`, `cargo xtask quick`, `cargo xtask
selftest` and `cargo test -p xtask`.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

